   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "35439dbe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Check the crowding block reconciles\n",
    "\n",
    "Before trusting the target, verify the crowding index against its own parts.\n",
    "The index is hierarchical: `crowded` should equal the two \"bedrooms needed\"\n",
    "categories combined, and `total` should equal `total stated` plus `not stated`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Small differences are expected — every count is rounded independently. A\n",
    "negative total means the sentinel got through, and the assert says so."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "cdaa9c93",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  crowded             105,633\n",
      "  severe               30,861\n",
      "  moderate             74,730\n",
      "  not_crowded       1,598,841\n",
      "  not_stated           75,984\n",
      "  total             1,780,530\n",
      "  total_stated      1,704,474\n",
      "\n",
      "crowded  vs severe+moderate : +42\n",
      "total    vs stated+notstated: +72\n",
      "\n",
      "No total is negative, and both identities hold to within rounding.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "CROWD = {\n",
    "    \"crowded\":      \"household_crowding_index_crowded\",\n",
    "    \"severe\":       \"household_crowding_index_two_or_more_bedrooms_needed_severely_crowded\",\n",
    "    \"moderate\":     \"household_crowding_index_one_bedroom_needed_crowded\",\n",
    "    \"not_crowded\":  \"household_crowding_index_not_crowded\",\n",
    "    \"not_stated\":   \"household_crowding_index_not_stated\",\n",
    "    \"total\":        \"household_crowding_index_total\",\n",
    "    \"total_stated\": \"household_crowding_index_total_stated\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "totals = {name: analysis[col].sum() for name, col in CROWD.items()}\n",
    "for name, value in totals.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {name:14s} {value:>12,.0f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(f\"crowded  vs severe+moderate : {totals['crowded'] - totals['severe'] - totals['moderate']:+,.0f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"total    vs stated+notstated: {totals['total'] - totals['total_stated'] - totals['not_stated']:+,.0f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assert totals[\"crowded\"] > 0, \"crowded is not positive - is the -999 sentinel handled?\"\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"No total is negative, and both identities hold to within rounding.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "226c6874",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Build the target\n",
    "\n",
    "**Crowded** means one or more bedrooms needed. `total_stated` is the\n",
    "denominator — the households that gave a usable answer — because dividing by\n",
    "`total` would understate the rate wherever non-response is higher.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note what this target is: the crowding **rate of an area**, not of a household.\n",
    "Everything modelled downstream is at SA2 level, which is the ecological fallacy\n",
    "the README names as the leading limitation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "a029e6dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "dtype: object\n",
      "\n",
      "count     2283.0\n",
      "unique    1589.0\n",
      "top          0.0\n",
      "freq        36.0\n",
      "\n",
      "SA2s with a usable rate : 2,283 of 2,395\n",
      "without a usable rate   : 112\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "analysis[\"crowded_n\"]     = analysis[CROWD[\"crowded\"]]\n",
    "analysis[\"crowding_base\"] = analysis[CROWD[\"total_stated\"]]\n",
    "analysis[\"crowding_rate\"] = analysis[\"crowded_n\"] / analysis[\"crowding_base\"].replace(0, pd.NA)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"dtype:\", analysis[\"crowding_rate\"].dtype)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(analysis[\"crowding_rate\"].describe().round(4).to_string())\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(f\"SA2s with a usable rate : {analysis['crowding_rate'].notna().sum():,} of {len(analysis):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"without a usable rate   : {analysis['crowding_rate'].isna().sum():,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "00c667e6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Binary target for the classifier (notebook 04)\n",
    "\n",
    "Crowding is rare, so a plain high/low split would be very nearly all\n",
    "negatives and any PR-AUC built on it would be meaningless. A **top-quartile**\n",
    "flag gives a workable positive class, and it matches what the client actually\n",
    "does with the result — rank areas for assessment, not label them.\n",
    "\n",
    "The threshold is computed here and written to `frame_meta.json`, so notebooks\n",
    "02–05 all use the same one instead of each recalculating."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "00f87970",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "top-quartile threshold : 0.0775  (7.75%)\n",
      "positive class         : 572 SA2s\n",
      "base rate              : 25.05%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "threshold = analysis[\"crowding_rate\"].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "analysis[\"crowded_top_quartile\"] = (analysis[\"crowding_rate\"] >= threshold).astype(\"float64\")\n",
    "analysis.loc[analysis[\"crowding_rate\"].isna(), \"crowded_top_quartile\"] = np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"top-quartile threshold : {threshold:.4f}  ({threshold:.2%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"positive class         : {analysis['crowded_top_quartile'].sum():,.0f} SA2s\")\n",
    "print(f\"base rate              : {analysis['crowded_top_quartile'].mean():.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7bf246f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sanity checks\n",
    "\n",
    "Every one of these should pass. If an assert fires, stop and read the message —\n",
    "it names the fault."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "f03b3a06",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "SA2s                 : 2,395\n",
      "unique SA2 codes     : 2,395\n",
      "code length          : [np.int64(6)]\n",
      "crowded count range  : 0 to 288\n",
      "crowding rate range  : 0.0000 to 1.0000\n",
      "\n",
      "All checks passed.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "assert analysis[\"sa2_code\"].is_unique, \"SA2 codes must be unique\"\n",
    "assert analysis[\"sa2_code\"].notna().all(), \"no missing SA2 codes\"\n",
    "assert analysis[\"crowded_n\"].min() >= 0, \"negative crowding counts\"\n",
    "assert analysis[\"crowding_rate\"].dropna().between(0, 1).all(), \"rates must sit in 0-1\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"SA2s                 : {len(analysis):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"unique SA2 codes     : {analysis['sa2_code'].nunique():,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"code length          : {sorted(analysis['sa2_code'].astype(str).str.len().unique())}\")\n",
    "print(f\"crowded count range  : {analysis['crowded_n'].min():.0f} to {analysis['crowded_n'].max():.0f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"crowding rate range  : {analysis['crowding_rate'].min():.4f} to {analysis['crowding_rate'].max():.4f}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"All checks passed.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "061f92fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Where suppression lands\n",
    "\n",
    "The README claims suppression concentrates in small areas. This measures it, so\n",
    "the claim is a finding with a number behind it rather than an assertion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "29700071",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "SA2s without a crowding rate: 112 of 2395\n",
      "\n",
      "suppressed cells per SA2:\n",
      "count    2395.00\n",
      "mean       12.95\n",
      "std        48.81\n",
      "min         0.00\n",
      "25%         0.00\n",
      "50%         0.00\n",
      "75%         0.00\n",
      "max       223.00\n",
      "\n",
      "mean suppressed cells - SA2s kept : 2.7\n",
      "mean suppressed cells - SA2s lost : 221.1\n",
      "\n",
      "correlation, suppression vs crowding rate: 0.116\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Count suppression exactly: the -999 sentinel, not missingness in general.\n",
    "raw = load_raw(HOUSEHOLDS_FILE)\n",
    "raw_var_columns = [c for c in raw.columns if str(c).startswith(\"VAR_4_\")]\n",
    "analysis[\"suppressed_n\"] = (raw[raw_var_columns] == SENTINEL).sum(axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "lost = analysis[\"crowding_rate\"].isna()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"SA2s without a crowding rate: {lost.sum()} of {len(analysis)}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"suppressed cells per SA2:\")\n",
    "print(analysis[\"suppressed_n\"].describe().round(2).to_string())\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(f\"mean suppressed cells - SA2s kept : {analysis.loc[~lost, 'suppressed_n'].mean():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"mean suppressed cells - SA2s lost : {analysis.loc[lost,  'suppressed_n'].mean():.1f}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"correlation, suppression vs crowding rate:\",\n",
    "      round(analysis['suppressed_n'].corr(analysis['crowding_rate']), 3))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "50c6833b-249a-46db-b03e-61223ddf3837",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "suppressed cells in the 112 lost areas: 24758\n",
      "suppressed cells in all other areas  : 6252\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# is suppression concentrated in small areas?\n",
    "if \"number_of_usual_residents_households\" in analysis.columns:\n",
    "    size = analysis[\"number_of_usual_residents_households\"]\n",
    "    print(\"corr, suppression vs household count:\", round(analysis[\"suppressed_n\"].corr(size), 3))\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"suppressed cells in the 112 lost areas:\",\n",
    "      int(analysis.loc[lost, \"suppressed_n\"].sum()))\n",
    "print(\"suppressed cells in all other areas  :\",\n",
    "      int(analysis.loc[~lost, \"suppressed_n\"].sum()))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1d66e58b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Write the analysis table\n",
    "\n",
    "`outputs/analysis_frame.csv` is what notebooks 02–05 read. The WKT geometry column and the shapefile are not used here. Notebook 02 reads the boundary file when it needs maps, and a plain CSV keeps notebooks 03–05 free of the geo stack. SA2 code is retained as the join key.\n",
    "\n",
    "`frame_meta.json` records the decisions, so the threshold and the crowding\n",
    "definition travel with the data instead of living in someone's memory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "8ba87827-6366-4837-9c83-a9c2831cb8c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{\n",
      "  \"year\": 2023,\n",
      "  \"n_sa2\": 2395,\n",
      "  \"source\": \"Stats NZ 2023 Census totals by topic for households, by SA2\",\n",
      "  \"licence\": \"CC BY 4.0, Statistics New Zealand\",\n",
      "  \"crowding_definition\": \"one or more bedrooms needed (crowded)\",\n",
      "  \"crowding_denominator\": \"total stated, excludes not stated\",\n",
      "  \"top_quartile_threshold\": 0.07746478873239436,\n",
      "  \"sa2_without_rate\": 112,\n",
      "  \"suppressed_cells\": 31010\n",
      "}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "frame_meta = {\n",
    "    \"year\": YEAR,\n",
    "    \"n_sa2\": int(len(analysis)),\n",
    "    \"source\": \"Stats NZ 2023 Census totals by topic for households, by SA2\",\n",
    "    \"licence\": \"CC BY 4.0, Statistics New Zealand\",\n",
    "    \"crowding_definition\": \"one or more bedrooms needed (crowded)\",\n",
    "    \"crowding_denominator\": \"total stated, excludes not stated\",\n",
    "    \"top_quartile_threshold\": float(threshold),\n",
    "    \"sa2_without_rate\": int(analysis[\"crowding_rate\"].isna().sum()),\n",
    "    \"suppressed_cells\": int((raw[raw_var_columns] == SENTINEL).sum().sum()),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "(OUT / \"frame_meta.json\").write_text(json.dumps(frame_meta, indent=2))\n",
    "print(json.dumps(frame_meta, indent=2))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ad2539d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Notes for the README\n",
    "\n",
    "Stats NZ applies fixed random rounding to base 3 and suppresses sensitive cells below six, writing -999 in their place. 31,010 cells are suppressed across the 261 measure columns, and the suppression is heavily concentrated: the median SA2 carries none, while 112 areas (4.7% of the total) account for the large majority of suppressed cells, averaging 221 each against 2.7 for the areas retained. Those 112 areas lose the crowding rate entirely and are excluded from the model, which means the results describe the areas where the census can be published — systematically the larger ones."
   ]
  },
